+# L4ZY menu plan for the settings assistant. GENERATED by distrib/tools/menus_plan.py
+# from data/menus.cfg and traduction.cfg at every release: do not edit by hand.
+# "## page | title | route" starts a page; the route starts at the main menu (Escape).
+# "== name" starts a section (its title in the page). Lines are numbered top to bottom.
+# On one line, " | " = side by side, left to right; "[ a / b ]" = a column, top to bottom.
+# {if ...} = only shown when the condition holds. "> page X" = the button opens page X.
+# checkbox / choice (radio buttons, "label"=value, side by side unless "one under the other") / slider / field /
+# flag / key / colours: the setting follows. "note:" = grey hint line, "status:" = coloured message.
+# Not resolved: loops over a count known only in game are shown once ("repeated");
+# labels computed in game show as <function>.
+
+# --- settings pages (Options) ---
+## options | SETTINGS | Options
+== (top)
+1. button "Search settings..." > page settingsearch
+2. button "Settings assistant (AI)..." > page assistant
+== What you see and hear
+1. button "Display" > page display
+2. button "Graphics" > page gfx
+3. button "Sound" > page audio
+== Controls
+1. button "Mouse" > page mouse
+2. button "Keys" > page keys
+== Game
+1. button "HUD" > page hud
+2. button "Friends and colours" > page friends
+3. button "Chat Translation" > page traduction
+4. button "Console and chat" > page console
+5. button "Recording" > page record
+== Settings file
+1. button "Import settings from another client" > page importsettings
+2. button "Edit autoexec.cfg" > page optionscfg
+3. {if MENU_resetask on} status: Really clear all your settings?
+4. {if MENU_resetask on} (button "Yes, restore defaults" : MENU_resetask = 0; exec "restore.cfg"; LOOK_r... | button "No" : MENU_resetask = 0)
+5. {if not (MENU_resetask on)} button "Restore defaults (clears all settings)..." : MENU_resetask = 1
+
+## display | Display | Options > Display
+== (top)
+1. button "Screen" : concat displaytab "=" 0 | button "Resolution" : concat displaytab "=" 1 | button "Advanced" : concat displaytab "=" 2
+== Window {only if tab "Screen" open}
+1. choice windowmode: "Exclusive Fullscreen"=1, "Borderless"=2, "Windowed"=0 (one under the other)
+2. note: Borderless: Alt+Tab and a second screen work without closing the game.
+3. {if "Borderless" chosen (windowmode 2) and fsaa > 0} note: Borderless at a chosen resolution needs FSAA at -1 or 0 (Advanced).
+4. {if "Borderless" chosen (windowmode 2) and not (fsaa > 0)} checkbox "Borderless at the chosen resolution (stretched, Windows unchanged)" borderlessres
+5. {if "Borderless" chosen (windowmode 2) and not (fsaa > 0) and "Borderless at the chosen resolution (stretched, Windows unchanged)" ticked (borderlessres)} checkbox "Keep proportions (black bars)" borderlessaspect
+6. {if "Borderless" chosen (windowmode 2) and not "Borderless at the chosen resolution (stretched, Windows unchanged)" ticked (borderlessres) or fsaa > 0} status: Borderless: the game uses the monitor size (<desktopw>x<desktoph>).
+7. {if not ("Borderless" chosen (windowmode 2) and not "Borderless at the chosen resolution (stretched, Windows unchanged)" ticked (borderlessres) or fsaa > 0)} text "Resolution: <scr_w>x<scr_h> (Resolution tab)" (computed)
+== Picture {only if tab "Screen" open}
+1. slider "Field of View (default: 100)" fov
+2. slider "Gamma (default: 100)" gamma
+3. {if Windows HDR on for this screen} note: Windows HDR is on for this screen: gamma is not applied.
+4. note: HDR: Options > Graphics > HDR screen
+== Speed and latency
+1. {if tab "Screen" open} checkbox "V-Sync" vsync
+2. {if tab "Screen" open} "Low Latency (mouse read once the GPU catches up)" choice lowlatency: "Off"=0, "On"=1, "Strict (lowest latency, fewer FPS)"=2
+3. {if tab "Resolution" open and "Borderless" chosen (windowmode 2) and not "Borderless at the chosen resolution (stretched, Windows unchanged)" ticked (borderlessres) or fsaa > 0} status: Borderless: the game uses the monitor size (<desktopw>x<desktoph>).
+4. {if tab "Resolution" open and "Borderless" chosen (windowmode 2) and not "Borderless at the chosen resolution (stretched, Windows unchanged)" ticked (borderlessres) or fsaa > 0} note: The resolution below applies in Exclusive Fullscreen or Windowed,
+5. {if tab "Resolution" open and "Borderless" chosen (windowmode 2) and not "Borderless at the chosen resolution (stretched, Windows unchanged)" ticked (borderlessres) or fsaa > 0} note: or in Borderless at the chosen resolution (Screen tab).
+6. {if tab "Resolution" open and "Exclusive Fullscreen" chosen (windowmode 1)} note: Exclusive Fullscreen: the monitor switches to the resolution you pick.
