+# --- bots (local games) ---
+botperception: how the bots this game plays see and play: every bot of a local game (Bot Match), and online the bots the server gives to this game (the server shares the bots out among the players who play; each player's game plays its share with its own setting, so the bots a player without Tiny Apa gets play Classic; on an L4ZY server, a bot added as Tiny Apa stays Tiny Apa whatever this setting). 0 Classic (default): the normal Sauerbraten bots; they see on a very wide field (135 to 270 degrees depending on their skill), react the instant you appear and know where you are behind walls (they aim at your real position through walls for 3 to 4 s after losing you, and chase it). 2 Tiny Apa (work in progress): bots modelled on one real player's play, named Tiny Apa (Tiny Apa 2, Tiny Apa 3... when there are several; on an L4ZY server everyone sees this name, elsewhere only the player whose game runs them): bots that perceive like a player and play like a strong player measured from recorded games. They only see what a player would see on their screen (never through walls or behind them), notice you after a human reaction time, hear the sounds the game plays (shots, jumps, weapon switches, teleporters, jump pads; there are no footsteps) as a rough direction and distance, and can lose you, so hiding, flanking and surprising them work. They aim with fast flicks that often overshoot then correct, shoot as soon as the crosshair passes on the body (about 54 % hits with the instagib rifle at full level; more on a target that runs straight or stands still, less on one that keeps changing direction), dodge sideways under fire instead of rushing you, and jump little. After respawning they take their bearings for a moment before acting; when they lose you they keep watching the line where you went out of sight; in a duel they sometimes hold a low cover and jump to look and shoot over it; they cut corners when walking and search calmly. Level with botstylelevel, a different form each game with botstyleform. Advise Tiny Apa to anyone who wants bots that play like a strong human, or who finds that Classic bots see through walls and aim the instant they appear. No fps change; processor cost measured with 8 bots: about 0.02 ms per frame for all the bots together. No graphics profile changes it. Online they play at the skill they were added with (botstylelevel counts in local games only); they never see through walls, so they know less than Classic bots and give nothing to any player. To add a Tiny Apa bot on a server: Master page, Add bot: Tiny Apa, or /addbot <skill> tinyapa. Menu: main menu > Bot Match > bots play
